EastSun 20260929: "確認github版本是否有更新，有更新下載", then "現在套、編譯" (after being told of package 61's golden
behaviour: opening/closing Teach or Motor Test clears the all-homed flag, settings pages refused while running).
Same cumulative pass as MERGE-8b5a91b5 (check_and_copy.ps1 rules). Union of packages 60..67: 107 files --
NEW 22, OLD 81 (machine copy = a laptop version), LOCAL 4. This round the three-way base is each package's own base_<prev>
(= the laptop version merged here last time), not the machine git history: the machine copies of wb_serve.cpp /
WebBridgeServer.cpp / cinitial.cpp were themselves merges, so the history walk fell back to 261c25d.
LOCAL (for each: laptop->result == base->machine, i.e. exactly the machine's own changes on top of the laptop's file):
  cinitial.cpp                  clean -- TEMP-DOORS / TEMP-DOORS-2 kept
  cStateRecord.cpp              clean -- OPLOG copy line kept
  WebBridge/WebBridgeServer.cpp 1 conflict: the laptop reworded the comment of the token-exemption line (condition
                                identical); the machine's TOKEN-OFF lines below it follow -> laptop line + machine lines
  tools/wb_serve.cpp            1 conflict: both appended at the end of the file (laptop: main.home W906_MainHomeCommand;
                                machine: OPLOG) -> both kept, laptop's first, OPLOG last
  + one machine change inside the merge, wb_serve.cpp (package 62's Q2-OBS observer.get token check, same line):
    `W906_WEB_TOKEN_ENFORCE != 0 &&` in front -- observer.get is exempt in WebBridgeServer, so with the token not
    enforced its sender never becomes the holder and the Yield acts would still have answered not-operator.
    (No other server-side token check in 60..67: ControlOwner()!= / not-operator searched in every package file.)
Machine-tagged lines in the 81 replaced files (MT-*, IOWEB-*, ONSITE-1, LAT-1, MERGE-*, TEMP-DOORS*, WSFANOUT, TAKEOVER,
TOKEN-OFF, OPLOG, SR-WIRE): 4 files carry them, none missing in the laptop's copy. MachineType.h is not in 60..67.
Package 67 (docs, RULINGS_20260928 #6): the Index Z (M14 MTestZ1) Gali_* -> 1203 route is the laptop's; not redone here.
Backup before applying: D:\HT9045\_BACKUP_20260929_pre_pkg67 (system, config, IniData, Error, HT9045_Log, GPIB9045\system,
UnloaderInfo, runcfg; file counts equal). No wb_serve was running.
Behaviour now on this machine, per the package README: DoAllProcess front section per golden (InitialICCheck / AutoClean /
ART / OCR / CleanSocket run when their settings are on); main.home WS command; settings-page close tail per golden
(Configuration / Yield save switches the heater relay and sends ATC); Teach / Motor Test open-close clears all-homed;
settings pages refused while running; InArm place-to-shuttle, AutoClean, OutArm Z-safe checks per golden (package 64: first
place with someone at the machine).

Build: build_integ_ship_x86 --target wb_serve exit 0 (169 objects rebuilt), 0 errors; pe_truncation_check 178 complete. ctest not run.

